{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019hbn85Y3z3Nm9WPrw4fjAZ","type":"tool_result","content":"5:**Status:** draft scaffold. Pending: final palette hex values, typography selection, illustrator contract terms.\n49:## Color palette (LOCKED — change requires style-decisions.md ratification)\n51:*Pending final hex confirmation.* Working palette:\n55:| Navy | Primary stroke, headings | `#0B1E3B` | 85/70/0/50 | Most body illustrations |\n56:| Teal | Secondary stroke, diagrams | `#1F4A4E` | 70/20/45/50 | Diagram accents |\n57:| Brass | Key emphasis / ★ Fixed Point | `#B58B3E` | 0/30/70/30 | Sparingly |\n58:| Oxblood | ⚠ Navigational Hazards only | `#7A2E2E` | 0/75/75/50 | Never decoratively |\n59:| Cream | Background / paper | `#F5EFE4` | 0/5/10/5 | Body page color |\n60:| Fog | De-emphasized, captions | `#8A8D90` | 10/5/0/50 | Secondary info |\n65:- Color carries semantic meaning: brass = key, oxblood = hazard, teal/navy = structure, fog = de-emphasized\n89:- **Alt text** (100–250 chars) describing the illustration's content in terms of the pedagogical point it makes, not just visual appearance. Example: \"A network diagram showing five activities connected in a path, with the critical path A→B→D→F highlighted in brass. The parallel path A→C→E→F is shown in teal.\" NOT \"A bunch of boxes with arrows.\"\n127:- **Visual treatment:** brass-toned glyph at ~14pt equivalent (smaller than block-marker symbols which are ~18pt); inline-prefixed in source markdown (`> ⚓ **Worth Securing:** ...`); production renders the glyph in the brand brass color (`#B58B3E`) followed by the bold name and content.\n129:- **Color discipline:** glyph in brass; the rest of the callout in body navy. No additional colors.\n134:- **Border:** 1px solid navy (`#0B1E3B`), with 8px outer margin and 16px internal padding\n136:- **Header:** name (`Logbook Entry` or `Extended Analogy`) in display typeface, navy, slightly larger than body text; followed by colon and a single-em-space gap before content\n146:- **Layout:** mostly tabular for density. Recommended structure: navy section headers (e.g., \"Domain Weights\", \"Formulas\", \"Top Distinctions\"); content below in compact tables with brass for emphasis on ★ Fixed Points and oxblood for ⚠ trap callouts\n154:- **Color:** body text color in fog (`#8A8D90`) for de-emphasis, OR body navy if the cross-reference is part of an instructional thread that the reader should follow now","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"74693b26-41c1-4417-aff2-df156c6e1659","uuid":"49974916-3abc-45d5-a0bf-e0093d103cdf","timestamp":"2026-08-24T14:16:46.193Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5:**Status:** draft scaffold. Pending: final palette hex values, typography selection, illustrator contract terms.\n49:## Color palette (LOCKED — change requires style-decisions.md ratification)\n51:*Pending final hex confirmation.* Working palette:\n55:| Navy | Primary stroke, headings | `#0B1E3B` | 85/70/0/50 | Most body illustrations |\n56:| Teal | Secondary stroke, diagrams | `#1F4A4E` | 70/20/45/50 | Diagram accents |\n57:| Brass | Key emphasis / ★ Fixed Point | `#B58B3E` | 0/30/70/30 | Sparingly |\n58:| Oxblood | ⚠ Navigational Hazards only | `#7A2E2E` | 0/75/75/50 | Never decoratively |\n59:| Cream | Background / paper | `#F5EFE4` | 0/5/10/5 | Body page color |\n60:| Fog | De-emphasized, captions | `#8A8D90` | 10/5/0/50 | Secondary info |\n65:- Color carries semantic meaning: brass = key, oxblood = hazard, teal/navy = structure, fog = de-emphasized\n89:- **Alt text** (100–250 chars) describing the illustration's content in terms of the pedagogical point it makes, not just visual appearance. Example: \"A network diagram showing five activities connected in a path, with the critical path A→B→D→F highlighted in brass. The parallel path A→C→E→F is shown in teal.\" NOT \"A bunch of boxes with arrows.\"\n127:- **Visual treatment:** brass-toned glyph at ~14pt equivalent (smaller than block-marker symbols which are ~18pt); inline-prefixed in source markdown (`> ⚓ **Worth Securing:** ...`); production renders the glyph in the brand brass color (`#B58B3E`) followed by the bold name and content.\n129:- **Color discipline:** glyph in brass; the rest of the callout in body navy. No additional colors.\n134:- **Border:** 1px solid navy (`#0B1E3B`), with 8px outer margin and 16px internal padding\n136:- **Header:** name (`Logbook Entry` or `Extended Analogy`) in display typeface, navy, slightly larger than body text; followed by colon and a single-em-space gap before content\n146:- **Layout:** mostly tabular for density. Recommended structure: navy section headers (e.g., \"Domain Weights\", \"Formulas\", \"Top Distinctions\"); content below in compact tables with brass for emphasis on ★ Fixed Points and oxblood for ⚠ trap callouts\n154:- **Color:** body text color in fog (`#8A8D90`) for de-emphasis, OR body navy if the cross-reference is part of an instructional thread that the reader should follow now","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
